# SCADA Digital Twin & Multi-Evidence AI Anomaly Detection System

## Implementation & Design Plan

A physics-first, multi-evidence anomaly detection framework for a single-tank water SCADA simulation, combining a Digital Twin, LSTM-Autoencoder, deterministic policy rules, and communication integrity monitoring into a hybrid fusion engine.

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Physical Parameter Sheet (Section IV):** The tank dimensions, pump flow rates, valve coefficients, controller gains, and noise parameters listed below are physically plausible starting values. Please review and confirm these numbers before Phase 1 coding begins, as every subsequent dataset value depends on them.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Storage Backend:** This plan uses **SQLite in WAL mode** as the local storage backend. SQLite is built into Python's standard library (zero external dependencies), supports concurrent readers with a single writer via WAL mode, and is perfectly suited for this single-process simulator architecture. The database file is fully portable and self-contained.

> [!WARNING]
> **Scope Boundary:** This plan explicitly excludes simultaneous multi-vector attacks, compromised physical actuators, complete compromise of all process sensors, and multi-variable replay attacks. These are documented as future work, not as weaknesses.

