```

### Frozen Threat Model

| ID | Attack | Description | Scope Boundary |
|---|---|---|---|
| **A1** | False Data Injection (FDI) | Attacker modifies sensor measurements (level only). | Actuator and flow telemetry remain uncompromised. |
| **A2** | Replay | Attacker substitutes current telemetry with previously recorded telemetry. | Single-variable replay (tank level + its original `source_time_s`). |
| **A3** | Denial of Service (DoS) | Attacker prevents telemetry/control communication from reaching the intended component. | Communication channel only; physical process continues. |
| **A4** | Authenticated Misuse | Attacker operates through a valid authenticated/authorized session but issues a command violating process safety constraints. | Single unsafe command; no credential theft modeled. |

> [!NOTE]
> The baseline prototype does not model simultaneous multi-vector attacks, compromised physical actuators, or complete compromise of all process sensors. These are documented as future work limitations.

### Frozen Design Principles

| Principle | Rule |
|---|---|
| Physics-First Sequence | Simulator + Twin validated (E0) before any AI code |
| Hardware Independence | Software-only, single-tank water SCADA simulation |
| Digital Twin Independence | Twin maintains isolated `H_twin` from prior predictions + control inputs; **never** consumes current observed sensor readings (Option B: per-scenario reinitialization) |
| AI Training Boundary | LSTM-AE trained exclusively on normal operational data including legitimate transients + sensor noise |
| Time-Series Split Integrity | Scenario-based splitting only; no random row splitting |
| Storage Backend | SQLite in WAL mode — zero-dependency, portable, single-file database; ideal for single-process simulator with concurrent dashboard reads |

