## III. SQLite Schema Design

### Database file: `scada_ids.db`

SQLite database with WAL mode enabled (`PRAGMA journal_mode=WAL;`). Four tables replace the four MongoDB collections.

### Table 1: `scada_telemetry`

Raw process/SCADA observations. One row per timestep per scenario.

| Category | Field | Type | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Identity** | `scenario_id` | String | Entire trajectory ID (e.g., `"N_001"`, `"A1_005"`) |
| | `sequence_id` | Integer | Incremental counter within scenario |
| **Time** | `simulation_time_s` | Float | Deterministic simulation clock (seconds) |
| | `source_time_s` | Float | Time the virtual sensor generated the reading (seconds) |
| | `data_age_ms` | Integer | Derived: `(simulation_time_s - source_time_s) * 1000` |
| **Communication** | `packet_received` | Boolean | `true` if telemetry arrived |
| | `communication_status` | String | `"NORMAL"`, `"DEGRADED"`, `"BLOCKED"` |
| **Operating State** | `operating_condition` | String | Context tag (e.g., `"Normal_Load"`, `"Setpoint_Change"`) |
| | `tank_level_setpoint` | Float | Target level in meters |
| **Physical Process** | `tank_level_observed` | Float | Observed/reported tank level H (meters) |
| | `q_in` | Float | Volumetric inflow (m³/s) |
| | `q_out` | Float | Volumetric outflow (m³/s) |
| **Actuation** | `pump_command` | Integer | Requested pump status (1=ON, 0=OFF) |
| | `pump_state` | Integer | Actual pump execution (1=ON, 0=OFF) |
| | `valve_command` | Float | Requested valve position (0.0–100.0 %) |
| | `valve_state` | Float | Actual valve position (0.0–100.0 %) |
| | `control_command` | String | Structured payload (e.g., `"VALVE_SET_80"`) |
| **Cyber/Auth** | `user_id` | String | Operator identity |
| | `user_role` | String | Operator role |
| | `is_authenticated` | Boolean | Identity clearance |
| | `is_authorized` | Boolean | Command permission |
| **Ground Truth** | `attack_type` | String | `"None"`, `"FDI"`, `"Replay"`, `"DoS"`, `"Auth_Misuse"` |
| *(Hidden from models)* | `attack_parameter` | Float | Scale of anomaly (e.g., bias=0.05) |
| | `ground_truth` | Integer | 0=Normal, 1=Anomaly |
| | `replay_source_sequence_id` | Integer/null | Original sequence_id for replay; `null` otherwise |

**SQL definition:**
```sql
CREATE TABLE scada_telemetry (
    scenario_id TEXT NOT NULL,
    sequence_id INTEGER NOT NULL,
    simulation_time_s REAL NOT NULL,
    source_time_s REAL NOT NULL,
    data_age_ms INTEGER NOT NULL,
    packet_received INTEGER NOT NULL,          -- 0/1 boolean
    communication_status TEXT NOT NULL,
    operating_condition TEXT NOT NULL,
    tank_level_setpoint REAL NOT NULL,
    tank_level_observed REAL NOT NULL,
    q_in REAL NOT NULL,
    q_out REAL NOT NULL,
    pump_command INTEGER NOT NULL,
    pump_state INTEGER NOT NULL,
    valve_command REAL NOT NULL,
    valve_state REAL NOT NULL,
    control_command TEXT,
    user_id TEXT,
    user_role TEXT,
    is_authenticated INTEGER,                  -- 0/1 boolean
    is_authorized INTEGER,                     -- 0/1 boolean
    attack_type TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'None',
    attack_parameter REAL,
    ground_truth INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,
    replay_source_sequence_id INTEGER,
    PRIMARY KEY (scenario_id, sequence_id)
);
CREATE INDEX idx_telemetry_scenario ON scada_telemetry(scenario_id);
CREATE INDEX idx_telemetry_attack ON scada_telemetry(attack_type);
```

