## IV. Physical Parameter Sheet

> [!IMPORTANT]
> These parameters define the entire physical simulation. All values must be frozen before Phase 1 coding begins.

### Tank Parameters

| Parameter | Symbol | Value | Unit | Rationale |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Cross-sectional area | $A$ | 2.0 | m² | Cylindrical tank ≈ 1.6 m diameter |
| Maximum height | $H_{max}$ | 2.5 | m | Typical small industrial tank |
| Initial level | $H_0$ | 1.0 | m | 40% fill — room for transients |
| Critical low level | $H_{crit,low}$ | 0.3 | m | Below this: pump cavitation risk |
| Critical high level | $H_{crit,high}$ | 2.3 | m | Above this: overflow risk |
| Overflow level | $H_{overflow}$ | 2.5 | m | Physical ceiling |

### Pump Parameters

| Parameter | Symbol | Value | Unit | Rationale |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Maximum inflow | $Q_{in,max}$ | 0.005 | m³/s | 5 L/s ≈ 80 GPM (small industrial pump) |
| Minimum inflow (when ON) | $Q_{in,min}$ | 0.005 | m³/s | ON/OFF pump (no variable speed) |
| Pump response delay | $\tau_{pump}$ | 2.0 | s | Mechanical inertia |
| Pump behavior | — | ON/OFF | — | Binary; no partial flow |

### Valve Parameters

| Parameter | Symbol | Value | Unit | Rationale |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Valve range | — | 0–100 | % | Continuously variable |
| Flow coefficient | $C_v$ | 0.004 | m³/s | Max outflow at 100% opening |
| Outflow model | — | $Q_{out} = C_v \cdot (V\%/100) \cdot \sqrt{H}$ | — | Gravity-driven, valve-throttled |
| Valve response time | $\tau_{valve}$ | 1.5 | s | Actuator slew rate |
| Safe valve position | $V_{safe}$ | 0.0 | % | Fail-safe: fully closed |

### Controller Parameters

| Parameter | Symbol | Value | Unit | Rationale |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Setpoint | $H_{sp}$ | 1.0 | m | Nominal operating level |
| Control interval | $T_c$ | 1.0 | s | Matches Δt |
| Control law | — | Hysteresis (bang-bang) | — | Simple, deterministic, reproducible |
| Pump ON threshold | $H_{sp} - d$ | 0.8 | m | Pump turns ON below this |
| Pump OFF threshold | $H_{sp} + d$ | 1.2 | m | Pump turns OFF above this |
| Valve setpoint | — | Controller-determined | % | Adjusts to maintain outflow balance |
| Hysteresis band | $d$ | 0.2 | m | Prevents rapid switching |

**Fail-Safe Behavior (deterministic):**

$$\text{DoS detected} \Rightarrow \text{Pump} = \text{OFF},\quad \text{Valve} = V_{safe} = 0\%$$

### Simulation Parameters

| Parameter | Symbol | Value | Unit | Rationale |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Time step | $\Delta t$ | 1.0 | s | 1 Hz telemetry rate |
| Scenario duration (normal) | $T_{normal}$ | 1000 | s | ~17 minutes per scenario |
| Scenario duration (attack) | $T_{attack}$ | 1000 | s | Same length for consistency |
| Sensor noise (level) | $\sigma_H$ | 0.005 | m | ±5mm Gaussian noise |
| Sensor noise (flow) | $\sigma_Q$ | 0.0001 | m³/s | ±0.1 L/s |
| Actuator delay | $\tau_{act}$ | 1 | step | 1-step command→execution lag |
| Base random seed | $seed_0$ | 42000 | — | Per-scenario: `42000 + scenario_index` |

### Stability Check

At steady state ($H = H_{sp} = 1.0$ m):
- $Q_{in} = 0.005$ m³/s (pump ON)
- $Q_{out} = C_v \cdot V\% / 100 \cdot \sqrt{H} = 0.004 \cdot V\% / 100 \cdot 1.0$
- Balance at $V\% = 100\%$: $Q_{out,max} = 0.004$ m³/s < $Q_{in}$ → tank fills slowly
- Controller cycles pump to maintain level within band

**Fill rate (pump ON, valve 100%):** $\frac{dH}{dt} = \frac{0.005 - 0.004}{2.0} = 0.0005$ m/s → 0.5 mm/s rise

**Drain rate (pump OFF, valve 100%, H=1.0):** $\frac{dH}{dt} = \frac{-0.004}{2.0} = -0.002$ m/s → 2 mm/s drop

**Time to drain from 1.2→0.8 (pump OFF):** ≈ 200 s — provides reasonable cycling dynamics.

