### Phase 3: Detection Engines & LSTM-AE

> **Goal:** Implement all four evidence engines and the LSTM-Autoencoder.

---

#### [NEW] `engines/physics_engine.py`

Wraps `digital_twin/physics_twin.py`. Computes $r_{physics,t}$ and normalizes to $S_p \in [0, 1]$.

#### [NEW] `engines/policy_engine.py`

Deterministic rules per Section II. Evaluates current state + command against safety constraints. Returns $S_c \in \{0, 1\}$.

#### [NEW] `engines/availability_engine.py`

Monitors `packet_received`, `communication_status`, `data_age_ms`. Returns $S_a \in [0, 1]$.

---

#### [NEW] `models/lstm_autoencoder.py`

PyTorch LSTM-Autoencoder:
- Encoder: LSTM → latent representation
- Decoder: LSTM → reconstruction
- Input: window of `[H_observed, Q_in, Q_out, pump_state, valve_state]`
- Loss: MSE reconstruction error

#### [NEW] `models/preprocessor.py`

- Per-feature min-max or z-score normalization (fit on training data only)
- Sliding window creation (window size `W`, stride 1)
- Scenario-aware windowing (no windows spanning scenario boundaries)

#### [NEW] `models/trainer.py`

- Training loop with early stopping on validation loss
- Trained exclusively on normal scenarios
- Saves model checkpoints with version tags

#### [NEW] `engines/temporal_engine.py`

Wraps trained LSTM-AE. Computes reconstruction error → normalizes to $S_l \in [0, 1]$.

---

#### [NEW] `engines/fusion_engine.py`

$$S_{hybrid} = w_p \cdot S_p + w_l \cdot S_l + w_c \cdot S_c + w_a \cdot S_a$$

- All component scores pre-normalized to [0,1]
- Weights and threshold configurable per `experiment_runs` document
- Returns final anomaly decision

